  "actuatorLimits": {
    "source": "public/physics/marty2_servo_supplier_envelopes.json",
    "status": "source_backed",
    "mappingStatus": "confirmed",
    "notes": [
      "URDF effort and velocity values are retained in movingJoints for traceability but are not emitted as actuator limits because the current URDF uses placeholder effort=30 and velocity=6.29 values.",
      "Source-backed force limits are emitted to MJCF position actuators as forcerange per actuator only when that actuator has a mapped supplier variant and limitSelection explicitly names a supplier voltage row, torque field, and velocity field.",
      "Batch 12 production mapping now resolves current commandable actuator variants: hip/knee use FT1190M, twist uses FT90M, and arm/eye use FS90MG.",
      "MuJoCo position actuator XML has no supported velocity limit attribute, so velocityLimitRadPerSec is exposed here for the controller rather than written into the MJCF.",
      "Firmware kp/ki/kd remain controller references and are not direct MuJoCo kp/kv/damping values."
    ],
    "selection": {
      "operatingVoltageV": 5.0,
      "supplierVoltagePointUsedV": 4.8,
      "torqueField": "ratedTorqueNm",
      "velocityField": "noLoadAngularVelocityRadPerSec",
      "selectionPolicy": "nearest-lower-supplier-voltage-row-no-interpolation",
      "sourceRefs": [
        "mjcf_actuator_limit_selection_findings",
        "servos_docx",
        "ric_6_1_0_pdf",
        "ft90m_spec_pdf",
        "ft1190m_spec_pdf",
        "fs90mg_spec_pdf"
      ],
      "caveats": [
        "Marty-side operating voltage is source-backed as 5.0 V, but the checked FT90M/FT1190M supplier specs provide 4.8 V and 6.0 V rows, not an exact 5.0 V row.",
        "ratedTorqueNm is a modelling choice for continuous MJCF forcerange based on the meaning of the supplier field; stallTorqueNm is retained as metadata for later stall/current protection modelling.",
        "noLoadAngularVelocityRadPerSec is a source-backed no-load cap, not calibrated loaded response timing."
      ]
    },
